==Trivia==
*Coffin Zoge's taxonomic name, Canis Deadus Doornailus, means "Dog as dead as a doornail", and is a form of dog Latin. "Dog Latin" is a debased Latin intended to mimic the language by conjugating English words and including suffixes such as  "-us" or "-um" onto the end of otherwise ordinary phrases (e.g. Big Shark - Sharkus Maximus).
**The taxonomic name in its Japanese description, Kan'o Kegata Noinu (カンオ・ケガタ・ノイヌ), is a pun on 棺桶型の犬 ''kan'oke-gata no inu'', which translates to "dog of the coffin shape" or simply "coffin-shaped dog".
*Coffin Zoge is the only [[Doge]] variant whose Japanese name uses the word ''inu'' (dog) instead of ''wan'' (woof) or ''wanko'' (doggy/puppy).
*Unlike [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]] and [[Wall Doge]], Coffin Zoge doesn't jump before falling down.

